From 406bffb55beeb0c547c6b1baf3fca74900489bc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:09:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] F-8: tree crowns and stall awnings count for the play
 camera's sight

- world.js: Citadel's round and fruit trees' crowns are a sight core (from 1.95 m, 1.5 m round at
  scale 1), soft: counted once he has stood 0.6 s (camera.js), so walking past trees does not rock the
  view; the Hamalayi's pines get the pines' core (hamalayi.js).
- Zeelich's market-stall canopy and Desert Island's stall awning are scenery volumes the camera rises
  over or looks round (walkUnder: passed through while he stands under them).
- tests/camcover.mjs: the audit's five spots (hopscotch, the cliff plateau after a Continue, Lhar's
  door, Oku's stall, the trader's stall) checked against the drawn scene by ray; 16 seeded spots by
  round trees: in view, or read as hidden with his outline drawn, never read as seen while hidden.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012GFEakZyL3XxjZKHRj5dFg
